lattice 4 x 4^3 = 256 sites, 1024 links, SU(2) 3 d.o.f./link = 3072 real d.o.f.
basis: 6 0++ operators  ->  GEVP matrices 6x6 = 9.2 kB per configuration set (nothing)

[T] criterion boundary is kinematic, not dynamic: if the 2nd 0++ level is the
    two-glueball cut, then m2 = 2 m1 EXACTLY, hence rho^2 = 4 EXACTLY.
    So rho^2 <= 4 is satisfied *with equality* by a NON-atomic second level:
    a measurement returning rho^2 = 4.0 +- s cannot separate 'atom just below
    the cut' from 'the cut'.  Only m2 < 2m1 by >> s is evidence for an atom.
    => the L=4 verdict hinges on resolving m2 vs 2m1, i.e. on Delta = (rho^2-1)mu1,
       not on rho^2 itself (atom3: Delta=(rho^2-1)mu1 is the load-bearing object).

